  "limitations_and_boundaries": [
    "PairNorm prevents performance from dropping significantly with increasing number of layers, but it does not necessarily yield increased performance in absolute terms on standard benchmark datasets because shallow architectures (2-4 layers) are sufficient.",
    "The hyperparameter s for PairNorm was fixed at 1 for GCN and GAT due to resource limitations.",
    "Results for GCN and GAT under SSNC-MV are only shown for 0% and 100% missing rates due to space and resource limitations.",
    "PairNorm is evaluated only on node classification tasks; applicability to other graph tasks is not studied."
